<WebLayout title="Kylie's Cyber Sanctuary — Final Fantasy, Gundam & Raves" description="Kylie's 1998 shrine to Final Fantasy, Gundam Wing and the rave scene. Materia combos, mobile suits and warehouse flyers.">

  <div style="text-align:center">
    <h1 style="font-size:34px">Kylie's Cyber Sanctuary</h1>
    <p style="font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13px">~ Final Fantasy · Gundam · Raves ~</p>
    <p style="font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:12px">established November 1997 · still awake from Saturday</p>
    <marquee scrollamount="5" style="background:#800080;color:#ffff00;padding:3px;border:2px inset #ff66ff;font-family:'Courier New',monospace">
      ★ FINAL FANTASY VII ★ GUNDAM WING ★ RAVE TONIGHT ★ MATERIA COMBOS ★ MOBILE SUIT MODELS ★ SIGN MY GUESTBOOK ★ BEST VIEWED IN 800x600 ★
    </marquee>
  </div>

  <div class="web-columns">
    <div>
      <h2>Welcome!</h2>
      <p>
        Hi! I'm Kylie. This is my website. I like JRPGs, giant robots, and dancing in
        warehouses until the sun comes up. I have been on the internet since 1997 and I
        still do not understand how email works.
      </p>
      <p>
        My friend <a href="/web/">pants</a> helped me set up this page. He says my
        background is "a lot," which I am choosing to interpret as a compliment.
      </p>

      <h2>Final Fantasy VII</h2>
      <div class="web-panel">
        <h3>Entry #48: I finally beat Sephiroth</h3>
        <div class="web-post-date">Nov 03, 1998 // 02:42 AM</div>
        <div style="text-align:center;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13px;background:#000;color:#00ffff;padding:10px;border:2px inset #808080;margin:6px 0">
          ★ FINAL FANTASY VII ★<br />
          MATERIA · LIMIT BREAK · CHOCOBO
        </div>
        <p>
          Two hours of grinding in the Northern Cave and it is done. My party was Cloud,
          Tifa and Red XIII. Tifa with Deathblow and a Powersoul is completely unfair.
          I cried at the ending. I am not going to pretend I didn't.
        </p>
        <p>
          Current project: breed a gold chocobo and beat Ruby Weapon without using
          Knights of the Round. This may take the rest of my life.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="web-panel">
        <h3>Materia combos I actually use</h3>
        <ul style="margin-left:18px">
          <li><b>Cloud:</b> Enemy Skill + All, Cure + All, Restore</li>
          <li><b>Tifa:</b> Deathblow + Added Cut, HP Plus</li>
          <li><b>Red XIII:</b> Lightning + All, Enemy Skill</li>
          <li><b>Everyone:</b> Long Range on the back row, because I am not made of gil</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Also playing <b>Final Fantasy Tactics</b>. My calculator is broken and my
          chocobo is named after a Gundam pilot. Do not ask which one.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Gundam Wing</h2>
      <div class="web-panel">
        <h3>Entry #47: import VHS marathon</h3>
        <div class="web-post-date">Oct 30, 1998 // 09:15 PM</div>
        <div style="text-align:center;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13px;background:#000;color:#00ff00;padding:10px;border:2px inset #808080;margin:6px 0">
          MOBILE SUIT GUNDAM WING<br />
          [ DEATHSCYTHE ] // MISSION START
        </div>
        <p>
          A friend taped the Japanese episodes for me and I have been watching them on
          repeat. Deathscythe is obviously the coolest mobile suit. Heero has the emotional
          range of a brick, but the Wing Zero transformation makes up for it.
        </p>
        <p>
          My model shelf currently: Wing Gundam, Deathscythe, Heavyarms and a tiny
          Ball that I painted red. Next up is Epyon, if the hobby shop ever restocks it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="web-panel">
        <h3>Gundam watchlist</h3>
        <ul style="margin-left:18px">
          <li><b>Mobile Suit Gundam Wing</b> — five pilots, five personalities, one war.</li>
          <li><b>Gundam 0083: Stardust Memory</b> — the best opening theme, no contest.</li>
          <li><b>Gundam 0080: War in the Pocket</b> — short, sad, perfect.</li>
          <li><b>G Gundam</b> — giant robot martial arts tournament. Peak television.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Rave Diary</h2>
      <div class="web-panel">
        <h3>Entry #46: warehouse off the ring road</h3>
        <div class="web-post-date">Oct 24, 1998 // 04:15 AM</div>
        <div style="text-align:center;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13px;background:#000;color:#ff66ff;padding:10px;border:2px inset #808080;margin:6px 0">
          ♪ TECHNO / BREAKBEAT / HAPPY HARDCORE ♪<br />
          WAREHOUSE · 10PM TIL LATE
        </div>
        <p>
          Three rooms, one fog machine, and a sound system that made my teeth vibrate.
          The breakbeat room was the best. Somebody handed me a flyer for a New Year's
          party and I have already taped it to my monitor.
        </p>
        <p>
          Current tape: Orbital's <i>In Sides</i>, The Prodigy's <i>The Fat of the Land</i>,
          Daft Punk's <i>Homework</i>, and a compilation with a track that sounds like a
          modem dying. Perfect.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="web-panel">
        <h3>Rave flyers</h3>
        <p style="font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:12px;background:#000;color:#00ff00;padding:8px;border:2px inset #808080">
          SATURDAY 31.10.98<br />
          [ THE PLEASURE DOME ]<br />
          warehouse · 10pm til late<br />
          techno / breakbeat / happy hardcore<br />
          bring whistles · glowsticks · water<br />
          <br />
          "PLUR"<br />
          — see you in the fog
        </p>
      </div>

